<p><em>Autumn and Winter</em>, by the 16th-century Milanese painter Giuseppe Arcimboldo (1527-1593).</p>
<p>Arcimboldo assembled similar portraits from <a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2007/07/14/renaissance-surrealism/">seasons</a>, <a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2010/09/20/essential-characters/">elements</a>, <a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2015/08/10/you-are-what-you-eat-2/">food</a>, and <a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2007/08/16/the-librarian/">books</a>. Art historian Werner Kriegeskorte calls him &#8220;absolutely unique.&#8221;</p>
